==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|acordingli}}, equivalent to {{af|en|according|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈkɔɹ.dɪŋ.li/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/əˈkɔː(ɹ).dɪŋ.li/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-accordingly.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{lb|en|manner}} [[agreeably|Agreeably]]; [[correspondingly]]; [[suitably]]
#: {{usex|en|He was absent when I called, and I '''accordingly''' left my card.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Antony and Cleopatra|passage=We may the number of ships behold, and so proceed '''accordingly'''.|3|9}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1895|author=H. G. Wells|title=The Time Machine|chapter=X|passage=Now, I still think that for this box of matches to have escaped the wear of time for immemorial years was a strange, and for me, a most fortunate thing. Yet oddly enough I found here a far more unlikely substance, and that was camphor. I found it in a sealed jar, that, by chance, I supposed had been really hermetically sealed. I fancied at first the stuff was paraffin wax, and smashed the jar '''accordingly'''. But the odor of camphor was unmistakable.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1987|title= Hang On To Your Horses Doovers|author=Kerry Cue|page=5|text=From the Marvel Mixmaster to the Miracle Microwave, every time a new-fangled gadget has lobbed into the Aussie kitchen, Aussie mums have changed their cooking styles '''accordingly'''.}}
# {{lb|en|conjunctive}} In natural [[sequence]]; [[consequently]]; so.
#: {{usex|en|Our preparations were all finished. '''Accordingly''', we set sail.}}
#* {{RQ:Conrad Heart of Darkness|page=200|passage='''Accordingly''' a young chap wearing his hat over the left eyebrow, some clerk I suppose, - there must have been clerks in the business, though the house was as still as a house in a city of the dead, - came from somewhere up-stairs, and led me forth.}}

====Usage notes====
* In contrast to {{m|en|consequently}}, which tends to imply a closer, logical or causal connection, ''accordingly'' generally marks the connection as one of simple [[accordance]] or [[congruity]], leading naturally to the result that followed.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|consequently}}, {{l|en|therefore}}, {{l|en|wherefore}}, {{l|en|hence}}, {{l|en|so}}

